Feature: Trigger Update Testing Change Script
	Validating trigger updates in zendesk and changing dates when updates to triggers have been made. 
	This is purely a script to help update the existing trigger update view test and should not be run on continuous integration testing. 
	It should only be run locally by QA testers who are updating the update dates on the trigger view test.
	Disclaimer: This test only updates the trigger update dates. It currently does not take into account trigger name changes or similar. 
	Those changes will still need to be made manually on both this file and the trigger update view test file before this script is run to prevent additional errors.
	Please commit all resulting changes after script is complete.

Scenario: View Triggers and Make Changes
	Check all triggers for updates to their update dates and make changes to the trigger update view test for all triggers that have had their dates updated

	* if the trigger "TEST opportunity owner" does not have "2021-05-05T17:55:51Z" as its update date then the update date on "ZendeskTriggerUpdateView.prose" and "ZendeskTriggerUpdateChange.prose" should be changed
